From: sunrisepeak <speakshen@163.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 11:25:01 +0900
Subject: [clangd] An operation takes a module scan replayed moments ago as
 replayed

Each document update and each completion replays every memoized dependency
scan it looks up: every file the scan observed is opened and checked again.
For a scan whose global module fragment includes a platform or framework
header that is hundreds of files per keystroke and per completion, which on
Windows costs more than the answer.

A document update now takes a replay made in the last two seconds, and a
completion one made in the last thirty, as made for it. A file the editor has
open is never part of a memoized scan, and a watched file's change ends every
such allowance, so what goes unseen meanwhile is a file changed outside the
editor that nothing watches. A preamble build replays as before.
